  m_Name: PY_10_MIXED
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::CodeEscape.Programming.QuestionData
  id: PY_10_MIXED
  language: 1
  topic: Mixed
  difficulty: 1
  questionType: 4
  questionText: Which code prints only the even numbers in nums?
  code: 'nums = [3, 4, 7, 10]'
  answerFormat: 0
  choices:
  - "for n in nums:\n    if n % 2 == 0:\n        print(n)"
  - "for n in nums:\n    if n / 2 == 0:\n        print(n)"
  - "for n in nums:\n    if n % 2 == 1:\n        print(n)"
  - "for n in nums\n    if n % 2 == 0:\n        print(n)"
  correctChoiceIndex: 0
  monospaceChoices: 1
  acceptedAnswers: []
  caseSensitive: 1
  explanation: n % 2 is the remainder after dividing by 2, and even numbers have
    remainder 0, so option A prints 4 and 10. B divides instead, C picks the odd
    numbers, and D is missing the colon after the for line.
  hint: The % operator gives the remainder of a division.
